Assinment title: Visual Prompt Studio 1.1

Prompt: Create a digital sci-fi movie poster titled Beyond the Void, featuring an abandoned space station floating above a distant planet, surrounded by darkness, stars, and glowing debris. Place a small astronaut in the center facing the massive station to create a feeling of isolation. Use sharp geometric lines in the station and dramatic diagonal lines from debris and beams of light to guide the viewer’s eyes, contrasting with organic curved lines in the planet and clouds. Include rectangular metal panels, circular windows, and the curved planet as dominant shapes. Use positive space for the astronaut and station, while the surrounding negative space emphasizes loneliness. Combine smooth, reflective metal with rough, damaged surfaces and rocky debris to create texture. Use highlights and shadows to give the station and astronaut realistic volume and a three-dimensional appearance. Choose a dark palette of black, navy blue, and silver with bright cyan lighting to create a mysterious, suspenseful mood. Place the bold, futuristic movie title at the bottom, keeping the composition balanced and the text readable. 

Vocabulary Breakdown : 
Lines: The lines create a mark that guides the viewer’s eyes throughout the artwork, which helps create movement allowing them to look at all the poster. Diagonal lines are used in my poster to guide the attention of the astronaut and to the spaceship. 
Shape: The shape is the outlines around the objects, for example rectangles, squares, and circles.  As for my poster, the circular planet and the effect of the shape of the space station creates interest into looking into it.  
Texture: The texture allows you to describe how the surface feels or looks, for example smooth, rough, shiny, and matt. In my poster, the rocks coming off make the surface look rough, which creates an appearance that looks realistic. 
Volume: The volume allows the object to have an appearance of depth or three-dimension forms rather than leaving it look simple and flat. In the poster, shadows make the astronaut look like he's really standing on top of the space and makes the space station look big and right over the whole image.  
Contrast: The contrast is a difference between elements, for example dark and light colors and small or large objects. The poster shows this by the bright light in the background against the darkness of the space station creating contrast to make details stand out. 

 
